From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koalabuttz <27229333+koalabuttz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:16:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor: name the 16-bit angle factors

0.0054931640625 (360/65536) and 182.04445 (65536/360 as a float) turn
up as bare numbers wherever an angle is packed into 16 bits or read
back. com_math.h now names them DEGREES_PER_SHORT and SHORTS_PER_DEGREE,
each as a float (_F) and a double so every use keeps the type it
multiplied by, with static_asserts that each equals the literal it
replaces. cg_pose.cpp's local SHORT2ANGLE gives way to the shared name.

No value changes: the double SHORTS_PER_DEGREE stays 182.0444488525391,
the number the code multiplied by, which is not 65536.0 / 360.0. This
answers upstream issue 53.
